<title>SOUTH AFRICA: LANGEBERG LIFTS HALF-YEAR EARNINGS.</title>
<headline>LANGEBERG LIFTS HALF-YEAR EARNINGS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31,</p>
<p>1997 </p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   25.5	  vs 23.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 5.5	   vs 5.5  </p>
<p>    Attrib income	   41.1	  vs 37.3</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   57.7	  vs 54.1</p>
<p>    Tax			 16.6	  vs 16.8</p>
<p>    Interest received     1.2	   vs 3.2</p>
<p>    Turnover		  560.5	 vs 449.1</p>
<p>Div payable July 11</p>
<p>on register June 6</p>
<p>Full name: Langeberg Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The fruit and vegetable processor said market</p>
<p>conditions had become more competitive. For the second half, it</p>
<p>expects satisfactory home sales but the international market is</p>
<p>likely to weaken further.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
